>> title: Pork Chop in Tomato Sauce
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: pork, tomato, rice, hong kong, stovetop, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: ke jap jyu paa, 茄汁豬扒, pork chop in tomato sauce, tomato pork chop, pork chop with tomato sauce over rice
>> pairs-with: baked-pork-chop-rice
>> servings: 2
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: pound thin, season, rest 15 min
>> step.2: fry 6 min, both sides
>> step.3: same pan — simmer 8 min
>> step.4: chops back in 2 min, over rice

Pound @boneless pork chops{2}(6 oz each; to 1/2 in) and rub them with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @white pepper{1/2%tsp} and @cornstarch{1%Tbs}, then ~rest{15%min}.

Fry @&(~1)pork chops{} in @neutral oil{1%Tbs} in a #frying pan{} for ~fry{6%min}, turning once, and lift them out.

Simmer @yellow onion{1/2}(sliced thin), @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @ketchup{1/3%cup}(80 g), @canned chopped tomatoes{7%oz}(200 g), @sugar{2%tsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{2%tsp} and @water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) in the same pan for ~simmer{8%min}.

Return @&(~2)pork chops{} to @&(~1)tomato sauce{} for ~simmer{2%min}, spoon them over @steamed jasmine rice{3%cups}(450 g), and scatter @scallion{1}(thinly sliced) over.
